{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-41552",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, we decompose all of the terms into their various factors. The $(3x)(7y)$ in the numerator becomes $3\\cdot 7\\cdot x\\cdot y,$ and the $28y$ in the denominator becomes $2\\cdot 2\\cdot 7\\cdot y.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(3x)(7y)}{28y}=\\frac{3\\cdot 7\\cdot x\\cdot y}{2\\cdot 2\\cdot 7\\cdot y}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we cancel out all the pairs of common factors in the numerator and denominator. In this case, there is one pair of $7\\text{'s}$ and one pair of $y$'s.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3\\cdot 7\\cdot x\\cdot y}{2\\cdot 2\\cdot 7\\cdot y} & = \\\\ \\frac{3\\cdot \\cancel{7}\\cdot x\\cdot \\cancel{y}}{2\\cdot 2\\cdot \\cancel{7}\\cdot \\cancel{y}} & = \\\\ \\frac{3\\cdot x}{2\\cdot 2} & = \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}x\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the expression simplifies to $\\frac{3}{4}x.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
